---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import eva from '../images/eva.webp';
---

<Layout title="About - Rewild" description="Meet Ewa, your guide at Rewild - grounded in nature, rooted in practice.">

  <!-- Navigation -->
  <Nav />

  <!-- About -->
  <section class="bg-white pt-36 pb-24 md:pt-44 md:pb-36">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-12">
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-24 items-stretch">
        <div class="md:order-1 md:sticky md:top-32 self-start">
          <Image
            src={eva}
            alt="Ewa"
            width={1000}
            densities={[1, 2]}
            class="w-full h-auto aspect-square object-cover object-top"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="md:order-2">
          <h2 class="font-display font-light text-3xl md:text-4xl text-forest mb-10 leading-tight">
            Hey, I'm Ewa
          </h2>
          <div class="space-y-6 text-forest font-light leading-relaxed text-[1.08rem]">
            <p>
              I teach nature-based movement at Rewild.
            </p>
            <p>
              I grew up in the mountains of southern Poland, training a variety of disciplines from an early age - mainly slalom skiing, trail running, mountain biking, swimming, martial arts and basketball.
            </p>
            <p>
              This early immersion in sports gave me a practical understanding of the body and a deep passion for nature, adventure and movement.
            </p>
            <p>
              I studied physical education in the UK, where I was introduced to yoga and pilates.
            </p>
            <p>
              After several years of practice, I obtained yoga teacher certification in London, and Advanced Trauma-Informed Academy certification with Nordic Maha Yoga, Oslo.
            </p>
            <p>
              The story of Rewild goes way back to the 80s, when being in nature was a part of daily life - training, foraging, and having a lot of freedom to play wild.
            </p>
            <p>
              In my early thirties, I've experienced immense challenges that took almost a decade to recover from. It led to physical and mental burnout, feeling exhausted, overwhelmed and isolated.
            </p>
            <p>
              I felt lost as to how to solve my life situation, and gave up believing that things would truly turn around. There was no way to numb it or distract myself from it.
            </p>
            <p>
              It got to a point where I had to escape this everyday reality.
            </p>
            <p>
              Then, intuitively, I started to hike up local mountains straight after work, regardless of the weather, infusing physical practices with nature connection.
            </p>
            <p>
              The transformative effects of it were immediate, and it totally changed my life. You can read more about this process <a href="/the-story" class="font-semibold underline decoration-forest/40 hover:decoration-forest transition-colors duration-200">here</a>.
            </p>
            <p>
              I felt inspired to share these tools with others, and it led to the creation of Rewild.
            </p>
            <p>
              My approach to exercise incorporates a variety of methods with an emphasis on functional movement, recovery and injury prevention.
            </p>
            <p>
              I spend a lot of time in nature - sleeping, training, healing, being, exploring - it brings me back to balance, fills with life, beauty and inspiration.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <Footer />

</Layout>
